['A team compares index settings on different corpus snapshots. What makes attribution difficult?','Changed conditions','Only the index nicknames','Only report typography','Only user avatar choice','Corpus differences can confound the apparent effect of the tuning parameter.','Names do not explain data changes.','Fonts do not control experiments.','Avatars are irrelevant.'],
['What should accompany an index’s query-latency headline?','Quality and cost evidence','Only a larger logo','Only one successful demo','Only the longest vector','Speed alone omits approximation quality and operational costs.','Branding is not evidence.','One demo is not representative.','Magnitude is not an operating report.']
